/-!
# PT6: the training half of E6 as a number

Source: `review/flat_spectrum.md`, *What a part of the table determines*, PT6. `halfMask` holds the
4704 training cells of E6 at `p = 97` as the bits `a · 97 + b`. The run of the kernel in
`E6Half.certificate` shows that the shuffle of `E6Shuffle` produces exactly this number, so later
checks read the literal and do not rerun the shuffle.
-/

@[expose] public section

